  "contract_assessment": [
    "collect_field_heads is actual ordinary success-only operation/server seam. Raw transferred handles remain unowned on operation error or future cancellation. Baseline deliberately preserves this.",
    "Ordinary fallible profile/client setup still occurs after raw spawn before completion seam. Source-supported setup exposure is not exercised by these cancellation controls.",
    "open_tunnel success-shaped Result preserves skipped URI/template errors and discarded send errors. WSS uses exact old builder/connect chain with builder error still propagated.",
    "Both cancellation observations retain actual external TCP client and runtime; bounded destruction-channel observation precedes backup abort and final client close. Object destruction is not a joined task result.",
    "Completed peer is observed via is_finished before error collection, not credited as awaited join. Both primary and secondary failures are intentional typed post-exchange injections.",
    "CRLF template is rejected through real PreparedRequestTemplate validation and real profile literal-value validation, not an alternate parser.",
    "502 accepts no origin TLS failure substitute: response parser returns HttpConnectError::Rejected status502 before origin TLS. Facade maps proxy category and preserves source.",
    "200-close positives use real record_connects per-iteration TCP Drop, then independently repeat actual request/opening. Exact transport TLS code maps backend connect failure to TlsError Handshake holding btls::ssl::Error; facade HTTP and WebSocket categories retain it. This supports a forecast, not a measured OS/backend error-code assertion.",
    "Existing wire/capture expectations remain independent literals and capture-derived name orders. No protocol fingerprint or production DNS/TLS defect inferred."
